  "topIssues": [
    {
      "id": "I_kwDOH2Qg5s7tjcI4",
      "title": "RPC Performance: Prevent eth_getLogs memory exhaustion (Upstream Geth fixes available)",
      "author": "locoholy",
      "number": 768,
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/op-geth",
      "body": "### Description\nCurrently, `op-geth` is vulnerable to the same `eth_getLogs` memory exhaustion loop that hits upstream `go-ethereum` when serving wide block ranges. Unbounded state scans can lead to severe memory spikes (OOMs) on RPC nodes, especially under heavy indexer load.\n\nMy team recently authored and merged the definitive fixes for this into upstream `go-ethereum`. We implemented bounded state scans and strict memory queue limits that prevent the node from crashing while keeping latency stable.\n\n**Here are our upstream PRs implementing these limits:**\n* eth: add admin_capabilities RPC method: https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum/pull/33886\n* * eth/filters: cap polling filter queues to prevent unbounded memory growth: https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum/pull/33885\n* * * ethclient: omit empty address/topics in RPC filter requests: https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum/pull/33884\n* * * * eth/filters: add optional getLogs limit support: https://github.com/ethereum/go-ethereum/pull/33881\n### Proposal\nSince `op-geth` is fundamentally Geth under the hood, we can help the execution client maintainers cleanly port these optimizations down to your architecture. This will dramatically save your RPC infrastructure providers from hardware overhead and network stalls.\n\nIf the core engineering team is interested in syncing on this, we are happy to put together a technical proposal (or RetroPGF submission) to implement these safeguards natively for Optimism. Let us know who to coordinate with!",
      "createdAt": "2026-02-24T19:39:52Z",
      "closedAt": "2026-02-25T11:40:45Z",
      "state": "CLOSED",
      "commentCount": 1
    }
  ],
